Source code for running analysis

# Multi-Omics Factor Analysis (MOFA) (src/mofa)
MOFA2 integration of pseudobulk gene expression (11 cell-type views) with untargeted metabolomics (1 view, log2_na transform). Post-hoc Spearman correlation of latent factors with gonadal hormone concentrations.

| Order | Script | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | `mofa_input_inventory.R` | Sample/cell-type grid inventory, completeness assessment |
| 2 | `mofa_integration.Rmd` | MOFA2 model fitting, variance decomposition, factor characterization, hormone correlation |
| 3 | `mofa_factor_pathway_analysis.R` | ORA and MSEA on metabolite factor weights |
| 4 | `mofa_umap_exploration.R` | MOFA factor values and gene expression on UMAP |

## Shared Function Files (sourced from src/gene-metabolite/)

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `pseudobulk_functions.R` | (sourced from src/gene-hormone/)
| `metabolite_functions.R` | (sourced from src/gene-metabolite/)

## Key Outputs
All outputs are written to `results/mofa/`.

| Directory | Contents |
|-----------|----------|
| `results/mofa/` | Varianceplots, factor weight CSVs, hormone correlation figures |
| `mofa_model.hdf5` | Trained MOFA model object |
| `pathway/` | Factor-weight ORA and MSEA results |
| `umap-exploration/` | UMAP overlay figures |

